The bug was caused by the server incorrectly requiring a `Content-Length` header when the `Transfer-Encoding` was set to "chunked". According to HTTP/1.1 specifications, when using chunked transfer encoding, the `Content-Length` header should not be included, as the data is sent in a series of chunks. The previous implementation did not account for this, leading to a conflict and potential errors in handling requests with chunked transfer encoding.

